    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> unified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> and in 508/507 BCE created the democracy that let the citizen Assembly decide war, finance and law.</li><li>Its fleet won at Salamis in 480 BCE and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> turned into a tribute-paying Aegean empire.</li><li>Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> in 404 BCE and dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> after 338 BCE, it stayed the cultural capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>'s sack.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Athenian jurors and many officials were chosen by lot; from the fourth century a stone allotment machine, the kleroterion, was used to assign citizens to courts at random.</p></aside>
    </section>

