ponnesian War</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">338 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> defeats <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chaeronea-338-bce">Chaeronea</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">86 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a> storms <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> after it sides with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI</a></span></li></ol>
